    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hipatterns\n\n### Description\n\nHi, I'm currently working through the mini.nvim plugins. I would like to replace `todo-comments.nvim` with this plugin.\n\nIs there an idea to add a function to cycle through the found patterns? There is `MiniHipatterns.get_matches()` already, so we are most of the way there. \n\nI think of the following requirements:\n\n1. Go to the next/previous match in the file \n  1. Add an option `infinite` or so, that it will restart of the end/start of the file when at the start/end\n2. Go to the first/last match in the file\n3. Add a table parameter that contains the possible highlighters that are affected by the cycle. \n\nHere is the corresponding section in todo-comments.nvim: https://github.com/folke/todo-comments.nvim#jumping",
