            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe main purpose of 'mini.hipatterns' is to highlight parts of text. Although I understand the use case of wanting to jump through \"todo\" like comments, it is probably the only popular use case for which jumping makes sense.\n\nThe `get_matches()` helper should be enough to create custom function for jumping. It can be used to either compute relevant cursor position to jump to or populate a quickfix/location list (and then jump with `[q` / `]q` / `[l` / `]l`).\n\nIf you use 'mini.pick', there is a [dedicated picker located in 'mini.extra'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/77e20cd6ed80fdf1738c116c35da81e7d9ad997e/doc/mini-extra.txt#L177) that can also make a decent alternative to jumping.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
